Z||000009||olympic||11-22-1999||01:25 PM||||I went to bid on an 85 GT with 130,000 miles at an auction 2 months ago. The interion and body were good but the motor, trans, suspension, paint and exaust were in rough shape. I fully expected to get it for $600 or less but some guy paid $1400 for it. Theres also a guy about 40 miles north of me who has 3 fiero's for sale. An 86SE,87GT and an 88 coupe. Problem is that the guy is in no hurry to sell them. They have been sitting there for at least 2 years because he wants $5500, $6500, and $7500 respectively!!! There is also a Formula that a new teacher has been driving around my home town. One day I'm going to leave him a note asking if he's interested in selling.||||reg||1
Z||000010||mshill||11-22-1999||01:57 PM||||Recently, in my area (Sacramento CA) the Fiero supply has dried up.  Three months ago there were 4-6 Fieros in the paper every week ranging from $750 to $2500.  Yesterday, there was a single 87GT for $5000.<P>I am hoping I didn't get the last real deal in the area.||||reg||1
